Each vendored file keeps an Apache-2.0 header that also records the local
modifications: the package was renamed to `com.auralis.app.glass.backdrop`,
the Kotlin context parameter in `LayerRecorder.kt` was replaced by an explicit
parameter (toolchain portability), the `@Language("AGSL")` annotations were
dropped, and `LayerBackdrop` gained an `isRecording` guard so a glass surface
drawn inside the recorded subtree skips its own sample instead of drawing the
layer into itself (a native renderer crash on the glass Library/Settings
screens). The sources were vendored because the published `io.github.kyant0:backdrop`
artifacts require a newer Jetpack Compose than this project targets.
